WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.340
With summer blockbuster season in full swing,
it's harder than ever to keep up with all

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.380
the new footage being released for upcoming
films.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.610
New trailers are hitting the web every day
for movies you won't want to miss.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.130
To help you keep track of everything Hollywood
has in store for us, here's a look at the

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.109
recently released trailers that will absolutely
blow you away.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:23.109
First Kill

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:28.249
Hayden Christensen rushes to rescue his son
in the first trailer for First Kill, which

00:00:28.249 --> 00:00:33.510
unites the former Star Wars actor with Bruce
Willis in an intense, action-heavy thriller.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.640
The movie stars Christensen as a Wall Street
broker who brings his wife and son to a remote

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.260
cabin in the woods for a vacation—only for
his son to end up kidnapped, leading to him

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.860
teaming up with Willis' police chief to rescue
the boy.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.260
Look for it July 21.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.460
Brigsby Bear

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:57.790
Things get very weird very quickly in the
trailer for Brigsby Bear, a bizarre dramedy

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.400
starring Saturday Night Live's Kyle Mooney.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.570
Mooney plays James, a man who's been the sole
audience member for the children's TV show

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:06.760
Brigsby Bear Adventures.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:12.430
When the show ends, James sets out to give
the story an ending himself, but he must learn

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.720
to cope with an outside world he knows nothing
about.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.740
Claire Danes, Mark Hamill, and Greg Kinnear
round out the supporting cast.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.130
Kidnap

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:27.390
Halle Berry gets the Taken treatment in Kidnap,
in which she stars as Karla, a woman who goes

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.900
on a mission to rescue her son after he's
kidnapped at an amusement park.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.840
The trailer ramps up into a high-stakes highway
chase with enough explosive visuals to leave

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.370
you ready to see more on August 4.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.450
Detroit

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:46.360
This trailer for Kathryn Bigelow's upcoming
thriller Detroit features a tension-soaked

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.360
look at the Detroit riots in the summer of
1967.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.490
John Boyega stars as a young security guard
caught in the aftermath of the Algiers Motel

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.250
incident, in which three young black men were
killed by police.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.690
The trailer knows exactly when it should change
gears to keep viewers' hearts pumping, and

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.920
it looks like another powerful drama from
the director of the Hurt Locker.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.289
Look for it August 4.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:11.680
American Assassin

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.790
Teen Wolf vet Dylan O'Brien takes a much more
dramatic turn in American Assassin, playing

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:22.420
a young man who becomes a CIA-trained killer
after his girlfriend is murdered in a terrorist

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:23.420
attack.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.019
Taylor Kitsch and Michael Keaton co-star in
this action thriller that looks like it hits

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:29.390
all the right notes.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.950
The trailer teases the film's action and the
characters' motivations without giving too

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:40.099
much away, leaving lots for audiences to enjoy
when the movie arrives in September.

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:41.299
Stronger

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:46.599
Jake Gyllenhaal stars in Stronger as Jeff
Bauman, a real-life victim of the Boston marathon

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:50.939
bombing who lost both of his legs while waiting
for his girlfriend at the finish line.

00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:55.879
Bauman published a memoir on his journey to
walk again, which serves as the basis for

00:02:55.879 --> 00:02:57.140
the movie's script.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:03.260
Gyllenhaal has repeatedly demonstrated a chameleon-like
ability to dissolve into his roles, and that

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.819
seems to be the case once again in Stronger.

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:10.889
The movie is sure to be a tearjerker, but
also promises to be an inspiring trip to the

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:11.889
theater.

00:03:11.889 --> 00:03:14.379
Look for it on September 22.

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:15.469
American Made

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:21.209
Tom Cruise does Tom Cruise things in the trailer
for his upcoming action film American Made,

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:26.459
which features the star as real-life pilot
Barry Seal, a drug smuggler recruited by the

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:31.879
CIA to help fight against the communist threat
in Central America in the 1980s.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:36.529
Cruise apparently flew all the planes for
real, even at one point stepping away from

00:03:36.529 --> 00:03:42.030
the controls to film a stunt despite the fact
that he was totally alone in the aircraft,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.599
because he's Tom Cruise.

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:47.879
The movie also reunites him with Edge of Tomorrow
director Doug Liman.

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:50.559
Strap in on September 29.

00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:51.559
Flatliners

00:03:51.559 --> 00:03:56.359
If you had reservations about the upcoming
Flatliners remake, this trailer should set

00:03:56.359 --> 00:03:57.359
you at ease.

00:03:57.359 --> 00:04:02.219
A new cast is featured this follow-up to the
'80s sci-fi flick, with Ellen Page, Diego

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:08.069
Luna, Nina Dobrev, James Norton, and Kiersey
Clemons taking over as the medical students

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:13.499
haunted by the dead after flatlining—experimenting
with dying for a few minutes before being

00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:14.499
resurrected.

00:04:14.499 --> 00:04:19.410
Although we're oversaturated with remakes
and sequels nowadays, Flatliners looks like

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.650
it has the potential to honor the original
while holding up on its own.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.520
Take the plunge on September 29.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.520
Marshall

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.550
Chadwick Boseman is a man on a mission in
the first trailer for Marshall.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:37.650
The Black Panther star plays Thurgood Marshall,
the first African American Supreme Court justice,

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:42.340
seen early in his career as a young lawyer
fighting for justice on behalf of a black

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.590
servant accused of attacking his white employer.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:50.599
Boseman seems like a safe bet to be a big
part of awards season conversations over the

00:04:50.599 --> 00:04:55.720
next several years, and Marshall might just
bring him his first major nomination.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.199
We'll see when it premieres on October 13.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:00.520
The Foreigner

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.970
Jackie Chan shows off his dramatic side in
the first trailer for The Foreigner, a thriller

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:10.099
that finds the action star playing Quan, a
restaurant owner who's hellbent on revenge

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:13.189
after his daughter is killed in an IRA bombing.

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:17.870
The trailer makes it clear The Foreigner won't
skimp on the action, but the serious role

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:23.110
has a touch of Chan's Police Story roots—and
he proves he can still pull it off in this

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.110
clip.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.979
Thank You For Your Service

00:05:25.979 --> 00:05:30.550
Following three soldiers who struggle after
returning home from Iraq, Thank You For Your

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:36.520
Service delves into the weighty topic of PTSD
and its lasting effects on veterans.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:42.330
The film marks the directorial debut of Jason
Hall, who was nominated for an Academy Award

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.419
for writing American Sniper.

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:49.880
The movie is sure to be heavy, but for viewers
looking for timely, thought-provoking drama,

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.970
it's guaranteed to pay heartbreaking dividends.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.419
Look for it on October 27.

00:05:55.419 --> 00:05:57.129
Murder on the Orient Express

00:05:57.129 --> 00:06:02.199
The first trailer for the upcoming mystery
movie Murder on the Orient Express starts

00:06:02.199 --> 00:06:03.580
with a scream.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:08.870
Based on the bestselling Agatha Christie novel,
the movie's all-star cast, including Willem

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:15.210
Dafoe, Daisy Ridley, Michelle Pfeiffer, Penelope
Cruz, Judi Dench, Kenneth Branagh, and Johnny

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:20.289
Depp, should be enough to make you want to
head out for a mysterious night at the movies.

00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:22.539
Take the ride on November 10.

00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:24.219
Daddy's Home 2

00:06:24.219 --> 00:06:29.949
Will Ferrell and Mark Wahlberg are back in
Daddy's Home 2, the sequel to their hit 2015

00:06:29.949 --> 00:06:30.949
comedy.

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:36.150
Only this time, the pair have some extra help
from Mel Gibson and John Lithgow as their

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.150
dads.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:42.340
The trailer features some standout funny moments
from Ferrell and Wahlberg, but the real stars,

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.729
despite their brief screen time, are Lithgow
and Gibson.

00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:49.150
Check out the absurdity on November 10.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:50.150
Coco

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:55.349
Pixar is back to tug on your heartstrings
again with Coco, a film that follows Miguel,

00:06:55.349 --> 00:06:59.410
a young boy who accidentally travels to the
Land of the Dead.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:04.039
The trailer doesn't give away many details,
instead opting to use uplifting music and

00:07:04.039 --> 00:07:07.150
bright visuals to highlight the film's humor
and heart.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.749
Even if it doesn't reveal much, Coco's trailer
should be more than enough to get Pixar fans

00:07:11.749 --> 00:07:15.800
young and old excited for the movie's November
22 release.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.249
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle

00:07:18.249 --> 00:07:23.190
Jack Black plays a teenage girl in Jumanji:
Welcome to the Jungle, so you know it's going

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.080
to be interesting.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:30.169
Taking place in the same universe as the first
Jumanji film, it sees four teenagers transported

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:34.979
into the world of a magical video game, where
they find themselves stuck in the bodies of

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:36.639
the game's characters.

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:40.509
While the trailer doesn't explain much of
the story beyond the premise, it does tease

00:07:40.509 --> 00:07:47.550
a ton of action and one-liners and suggests
that this Jumanji could be a game worth playing…

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.300
and a movie worth watching.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.900
Head into the jungle on December 20.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.710
The Greatest Showman

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:58.509
It's easy to buy Hugh Jackman as the inventor
of show business in the first trailer for

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:01.979
his upcoming musical The Greatest Showman.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:04.150
Jackman steps into the role of P.T.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.639
Barnum, the man who defined show business
as we know it through his founding of the

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:09.849
Barnum and Bailey Circus.

00:08:09.849 --> 00:08:15.009
The Greatest Showman trailer uses Jackman's
inherent charm to gloss over some of the seedier

00:08:15.009 --> 00:08:20.340
aspects of Barnum's story, but while it may
not be historically accurate, it does promise

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.639
a dazzling reminder of the power of the human
spirit.

00:08:23.639 --> 00:08:26.580
Watch it Christmas Day 2017.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:27.580
Black Panther

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:33.950
Wakanda is officially our new favorite location
in the MCU after the gorgeous Black Panther

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:39.310
trailer, which introduces live-action audiences
to the mysterious country for the first time.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:44.920
Chadwick Boseman finally steps into the solo
spotlight, his supporting cast is stunning,

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.780
and the costuming and gorgeous visuals immediately
put the movie in an MCU league of its own.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:56.770
The only thing wrong with this trailer: the
movie doesn't come out until February 2018.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:57.770
Thanks for watching!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.520
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.780
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

